[32m+[m[32m## Long-Term Research Direction[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMy long-term goal is to develop robots that can work safely and intelligently alongside humans in busy and constantly changing environments such as commercial kitchens.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mI am interested in robots that can:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- navigate safely through crowded environments[m
[32m+[m[32m- distinguish between objects and understand their surroundings[m
[32m+[m[32m- anticipate human movement from behaviour[m
[32m+[m[32m- cooperate naturally with human coworkers[m
[32m+[m[32m- grasp and manipulate objects reliably[m
[32m+[m[32m- handle tools and ingredients safely[m
[32m+[m[32m- manage tasks according to human orders[m
[32m+[m[32m- monitor stock and operational state[m
[32m+[m[32m- manage battery and long-duration operation[m
[32m+[m[32m- maintain safe physical behaviour in unpredictable environments[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA kitchen is an environment where a wrong movement or grasp can be costly or dangerous. Because of this, I am especially interested in reliable perception, manipulation, human-aware navigation, and safe decision making.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMy biggest interest is not simply making robots execute predefined movements.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mI want to understand how a robot can:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**observe → understand → predict → decide → act safely**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEventually, I want to explore robotic systems capable of understanding human behaviour and cooperating with people more naturally, closer to the way human coworkers continuously adapt to one another.[m
